two rolls or sum==10 -> frame done, move next, reset pins_left=10. else (first roll <10) -> pins_left -= pins, 
stay in frame.

  - if frame == 9 (10th): handle fill balls: if first roll strike or spare (after two rolls sum==10) need fill 
balls. After enough rolls (2 if open, 3 if strike/spare), game complete.

- `score()`: if not complete -> None. Else compute using standard algorithm: iterate frames 0..9, for each get 
rolls from `rolls` vector flattened. Use index into flat rolls.



Simpler: store flat `rolls: Vec<u16>` and a method to know if complete. Compute score by walking frames.



