I will implement the BankAccount class to support opening/closing, deposits, withdrawals, and balance checks, while ensuring thread safety using the existing `synchronized` keywords and handling operations on closed accounts by throwing `BankAccountActionInvalidException`.

BankAccount.java
```
class BankAccount {
    private boolean open = false;
    private int balance = 0;

    void open() throws BankAccountActionInvalidException {
        synchronized (this) {
            if (open) {
                throw new BankAccountActionInvalidException("Account already open");
            }
            open = true;
            balance = 0;
        }
    }

    void close() throws BankAccountActionInvalidException {
        synchronized (this) {
            if (!open) {
                throw new BankAccountActionInvalidException("Account not open");
            }
            open = false;
        }
    }

    synchronized int getBalance() throws BankAccountActionInvalidException {
        if (!open) {
            throw new BankAccountActionInvalidException("Account not open");
        }
        return balance;
    }

    synchronized void deposit(int amount) throws BankAccountActionInvalidException {
        if (!open) {
            throw new BankAccountActionInvalidException("Account not open");
        }
        if (amount < 0) {
            throw new BankAccountActionInvalidException("Cannot deposit negative amount");
        }
        balance += amount;
    }

    synchronized void withdraw(int amount) throws BankAccountActionInvalidException {
        if (!open) {
            throw new BankAccountActionInvalidException("Account not open");
        }
        if (amount < 0) {
            throw new BankAccountActionInvalidException("Cannot withdraw negative amount");
        }
        if (amount > balance) {
            throw new BankAccountActionInvalidException("Insufficient funds");
        }
        balance -= amount;
    }

}
```

Note: The above assumes `BankAccountActionInvalidException` is a defined exception class (as referenced in the original method signatures). The implementation uses `synchronized` on all methods that access shared state to prevent race conditions, and checks `open` state to fail operations on closed accounts.
