I'll implement the BaseConverter class to convert numbers between bases using positional notation, without relying on built-in conversion utilities.

BaseConverter.java
```
class BaseConverter {

    private int originalBase;
    private int[] originalDigits;

    BaseConverter(int originalBase, int[] originalDigits) {
        this.originalBase = originalBase;
        this.originalDigits = originalDigits;
    }

    int[] convertToBase(int newBase) {
        // Step 1: convert original digits to a decimal (base 10) value
        long value = 0;
        long power = 1;
        for (int i = originalDigits.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            value += originalDigits[i] * power;
            power *= originalBase;
        }

        // Step 2: convert the decimal value to the new base
        if (value == 0) {
            return new int[]{0};
        }

        java.util.ArrayList<Integer> digitsList = new java.util.ArrayList<>();
        long remainder = value;
        while (remainder > 0) {
            digitsList.add((int) (remainder % newBase));
            remainder /= newBase;
        }

        // Reverse the list since we collected digits from least to most significant
        int[] result = new int[digitsList.size()];
        for (int i = 0; i < digitsList.size(); i++) {
            result[i] = digitsList.get(digitsList.size() - 1 - i);
        }
        return result;
    }

}
```
