The `sublist.h` content shown in the snippet already defines `List_comparison` and the `sublist` template function exactly as required by the tests, with no syntax errors. The `sublist.cpp` file (provided earlier) just includes the header and is fine. No changes are needed to fix errors.

Since no changes are required, I will simply output the current true contents of both files as file listings for confirmation.

sublist.h
```
#pragma once

#include <vector>
#include <algorithm>

namespace sublist {

enum class List_comparison {
    equal,
    sublist,
    superlist,
    unequal
};

template <typename T>
List_comparison sublist(const std::vector<T>& a, const std::vector<T>& b) {
    if (a == b) return List_comparison::equal;
    if (a.empty() && !b.empty()) return List_comparison::sublist;
    if (!a.empty() && b.empty()) return List_comparison::superlist;
    if (a.size() >= b.size() &&
        std::search(a.begin(), a.end(), b.begin(), b.end()) != a.end())
        return List_comparison::superlist;
    if (b.size() >= a.size() &&
        std::search(b.begin(), b.end(), a.begin(), a.end()) != b.end())
        return List_comparison::sublist;
    return List_comparison::unequal;
}

}  // namespace sublist
```

