I will implement the `Palindromes.generate` method to find the smallest and largest palindrome products in a given range, along with their factor pairs.

The method should accept an object with `min` and `max` properties (as typical for this exercise), compute all products of two numbers in `[min, max]`, identify palindromes, and return an object with `smallest` and `largest` containing `value` and `factors` (array of `[a, b]` pairs).

Here is the updated file:

palindrome-products.js
```
//
// This is only a SKELETON file for the 'Palindrome Products' exercise. It's been provided as a
// convenience to get you started writing code faster.
//

export class Palindromes {
  static generate({ min, max }) {
    const isPalindrome = (n) => {
      const s = String(n);
      return s === s.split('').reverse().join('');
    };

    let smallest = null;
    let largest = null;

    for (let i = min; i <= max; i++) {
      for (let j = i; j <= max; j++) {
        const product = i * j;
        if (!isPalindrome(product)) continue;

        if (smallest === null || product < smallest.value) {
          smallest = { value: product, factors: [[i, j]] };
        } else if (product === smallest.value) {
          smallest.factors.push([i, j]);
        }

        if (largest === null || product > largest.value) {
          largest = { value: product, factors: [[i, j]] };
        } else if (product === largest.value) {
          largest.factors.push([i, j]);
        }
      }
    }

    return { smallest, largest };
  }
}
```
