Actually, the above logic is still a bit convoluted. Let me simplify to a standard BFS/loop that respects the forbidden state and just does the right sequence: fill start, then alternate pouring/emptying/filling as needed. The typical algorithm for "two bucket" puzzle (with the extra forbidden rule) is:

- Fill start bucket (move 1)
- Loop:
  - If the other bucket is full, empty it (move++).
  - Else, pour from start bucket to other bucket (move++). (This automatically stops when start is empty or other is full.)
  - After pour, if start bucket is empty, fill it (move++).
  - Check goal after each change.
  - If we ever would end with start empty and other full, we instead empty other before pouring? Actually the forbidden state is *after an action*. So we must never perform an action that results in (start empty, other full). In the normal pour, if start becomes empty and other becomes full simultaneously, that's the forbidden state! So we must avoid that by, when start is about to empty and other is about to fill at the same time, instead doing something else? The instructions say: "After an action, you may not arrive at a state where the initial starting bucket is empty and the other bucket is full." So we must ensure our sequence never produces that. The classic way: if pouring would result in that exact state, instead empty the other bucket first (or fill start? but start is already empty). Actually if start is empty and other is not full, we fill start. If other is full, we empty other. So the forbidden state only occurs if we pour from a full start into a full other? No, other is not full yet. Wait: start empty + other full means we poured the last of start into other and other became exactly full. That is the forbidden state. So we must avoid that pour; instead, before pouring, if start is full and other is such that pouring all from start fills other exactly, we should empty other first, then pour. That avoids the forbidden end state.

Let me rewrite cleanly with that in mind.

TwoBucket.java
```
import java.util.HashSet;
import java.util.Set;

class TwoBucket {
    private int totalMoves;
    private String finalBucket;
    private int otherBucket;

    TwoBucket(int bucketOneCap, int bucketTwoCap, int desiredLiters, String startBucket) {
        int cap1 = bucketOneCap;
        int cap2 = bucketTwoCap;
        int goal = desiredLiters;
        boolean startWithOne = startBucket.equalsIgnoreCase("one");

        int amt1 = 0, amt2 = 0;
        int moves = 0;

        // Move 1: fill starting bucket
        if (startWithOne) {
            amt1 = cap1;
        } else {
            amt2 = cap2;
        }
        moves = 1;

        if (amt1 == goal) {
            this.totalMoves = moves;
            this.finalBucket = "one";
            this.otherBucket = amt2;
            return;
        }
        if (amt2 == goal) {
            this.totalMoves = moves;
            this.finalBucket = "two";
            this.otherBucket = amt1;
            return;
        }

        Set<String> seen = new HashSet<>();
        seen.add(amt1 + "," + amt2);

        while (true) {
            if (startWithOne) {
                // If pouring from 1 to 2 would create forbidden state (1 empty, 2 full)
                if (amt1 == cap1 && amt2 == cap2 - amt1) {
                    // would become (0, cap2) -> forbidden, so empty 2 first
                    amt2 = 0;
                    moves++;
                    if (amt1 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "one"; this.otherBucket = amt2; return; }
                    if (amt2 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "two"; this.otherBucket = amt1; return; }
                }
                // Pour 1 -> 2
                int pour = Math.min(amt1, cap2 - amt2);
                amt1 -= pour;
                amt2 += pour;
                moves++;
                if (amt1 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "one"; this.otherBucket = amt2; return; }
                if (amt2 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "two"; this.otherBucket = amt1; return; }

                // If bucket 1 empty, fill it
                if (amt1 == 0) {
                    amt1 = cap1;
                    moves++;
                    if (amt1 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "one"; this.otherBucket = amt2; return; }
                    if (amt2 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "two"; this.otherBucket = amt1; return; }
                }
                // If bucket 2 full, empty it
                else if (amt2 == cap2) {
                    amt2 = 0;
                    moves++;
                    if (amt1 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "one"; this.otherBucket = amt2; return; }
                    if (amt2 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "two"; this.otherBucket = amt1; return; }
                }
            } else {
                // start with bucket two
                if (amt2 == cap2 && amt1 == cap1 - amt2) {
                    amt1 = 0;
                    moves++;
                    if (amt1 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "one"; this.otherBucket = amt2; return; }
                    if (amt2 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "two"; this.otherBucket = amt1; return; }
                }
                int pour = Math.min(amt2, cap1 - amt1);
                amt2 -= pour;
                amt1 += pour;
                moves++;
                if (amt1 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "one"; this.otherBucket = amt2; return; }
                if (amt2 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "two"; this.otherBucket = amt1; return; }

                if (amt2 == 0) {
                    amt2 = cap2;
                    moves++;
                    if (amt1 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "one"; this.otherBucket = amt2; return; }
                    if (amt2 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "two"; this.otherBucket = amt1; return; }
                } else if (amt1 == cap1) {
                    amt1 = 0;
                    moves++;
                    if (amt1 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "one"; this.otherBucket = amt2; return; }
                    if (amt2 == goal) { this.totalMoves = moves; this.finalBucket = "two"; this.otherBucket = amt1; return; }
                }
            }

            String state = amt1 + "," + amt2;
            if (seen.contains(state)) {
                throw new IllegalStateException("No solution");
            }
            seen.add(state);
        }
    }

    int getTotalMoves() {
        return totalMoves;
    }

    String getFinalBucket() {
        return finalBucket;
    }

    int getOtherBucket() {
        return otherBucket;
    }
}
