I will implement the Binary class to convert a binary string to its decimal equivalent, handling invalid inputs by returning 0 (as is typical for this exercise). The constructor should store the input string, and `toDecimal` should compute the decimal value using first principles (powers of 2) and return 0 for invalid strings.

binary.js
```
//
// This is only a SKELETON file for the 'Binary' exercise. It's been provided as a
// convenience to get you started writing code faster.
//

export class Binary {
  constructor(input) {
    this.input = input;
  }

  toDecimal() {
    if (!/^[01]+$/.test(this.input)) {
      return 0;
    }

    let decimal = 0;
    const length = this.input.length;
    for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) {
      const bit = parseInt(this.input[length - 1 - i], 10);
      decimal += bit * Math.pow(2, i);
    }
    return decimal;
  }
}
```
