Simpler: collect groups in a slice from LSB to MSB (as we do), then iterate the slice in reverse order setting continuation bits appropriately: the first byte output (MSB) should have 0x80, all until the last should have 0x80, and the last (LSB) should not. But currently we set 0x80 on all except the last *in the original slice*, then reverse, which means after reversal the *first* output byte (which was last in original) does NOT have 0x80, and the rest do. That's exactly inverted. So we should instead: collect groups LSB->MSB, then reverse the slice, then set 0x80 on all except the last *in the reversed slice* (i.e., all bytes except the final one). Or easier: don't reverse, but build from MSB to LSB.

